<LegalLayout
  title="Return & Refund Policy"
  description="How returns, refunds, cancellations, and warranty claims work for products purchased through authorized resellers."
>
  <h2>1. We are not the seller</h2>
  <p>
    Davis Weather Station is an independent directory. We do not sell products, process payments, ship orders, or
    issue refunds. All purchases are made directly with the authorized reseller you choose. The reseller’s own
    return, refund, cancellation, and warranty policies apply to your order.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Reseller policies govern</h2>
  <p>
    Return windows, restocking fees, condition requirements, original-packaging rules, and refund methods vary by
    reseller and by country. Review the reseller’s terms before ordering, and contact the reseller directly if you
    need to return or cancel an order.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Damaged, defective, or incorrect items</h2>
  <p>
    If your order arrives damaged, defective, or different from what you ordered, contact the reseller promptly.
    Keep the packaging, accessories, and proof of purchase. The reseller will explain the inspection, replacement,
    repair, or refund process.
  </p>
  <p>
    Most Davis Instruments products carry a limited manufacturer warranty. Warranty coverage and procedures are
    handled by the reseller or an authorized repair center. See our <a href="/resellers/">reseller directory</a> for
    listings that may include repair services.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Cancellations</h2>
  <p>
    Cancellation rights depend on the reseller’s terms and on your local consumer law. Contact the reseller as soon
    as possible. Once an order has shipped or a custom configuration has been built, cancellation may no longer be
    possible or may incur fees.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Returns and shipping costs</h2>
  <p>
    Unless the reseller or applicable law says otherwise, you may be responsible for return shipping costs and for
    the risk of loss during return transit. Use a trackable service and keep proof of shipment. The reseller may
    require a return authorization number before accepting a return.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Refund timing and method are set by the reseller and may depend on the payment provider, inspection, and local
    law. Refunds may be issued to the original payment method, as store credit, or by another method permitted by
    the reseller’s policy. Shipping charges may be non-refundable.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Chargebacks and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    If you have a problem with an order, contact the reseller first. A payment dispute or chargeback should be a last
    resort after good-faith attempts to resolve the issue. We cannot influence a reseller’s payment or refund
    decision.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Warranty claims</h2>
  <p>
    Warranty claims are handled by the reseller, the manufacturer, or an authorized repair center, subject to the
    product’s warranty terms and your statutory rights. Keep your receipt and product serial number. Warranty
    coverage may vary by region and product.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Our role</h2>
  <p>
    We can help you identify the reseller you used or provide publicly available contact details, but we cannot
    process returns, refunds, or warranty claims on a reseller’s behalf.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Need help finding the right reseller contact? Use the <a href="/resellers/">reseller directory</a> or our{' '}
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
